      "message": "Can you explain how you chose this? I\u0027d imagine that you evaluated the likely number of subclasses of NetworkCallback that the app (more specifically, the app code that uses this particular ConnectivityManager instance) is likely to use.\n\nAlso explain what happens when the app uses more than that - presumably there\u0027s some cache thrashing, but that only implements the performance of registerDefaultNetworkCallback and related methods, which is not latency-sensitive?\n\nDo you have any idea how long it takes to scan a particular NC subclass and populate an entry.",
